","ma-c-a17f828085d956f5ddcd","ma-c-aa0dad6e82c84b0aeff8","ma-c-b190e8186e373b4619b1","ma-c-c4bfe9579650b815ce8c","ma-c-cd39e53bd9f25e2357eb","ma-c-d9f501651c53edce46fb","ma-c-da7c98c65456ac841089","ma-c-dfd9eb1d1d7e92142a0d","ma-c-e4a4507d161844c14eca","ma-c-fb64a661e711ab32338c"],"leaves":["ma-c-038ce650729ac56972ab","ma-c-1d7931448180db9eae37","ma-c-1fc414740e4d58773f88","ma-c-236d775a018e1d1e6e55","ma-c-28d0e02433e91dbdaea7","ma-c-387a6ac40920c0ab63b1","ma-c-3984531170f982756695","ma-c-4414e9013e2ea5249ea5","ma-c-4d5d5b5bf63e0df8aa1f","ma-c-5e03aa7319b9ee079e54","ma-c-631fa6d2455774cdb1e5","ma-c-6949d672ccad43c12542","ma-c-786fcb0a1b188fd7c34e","ma-c-7e39eabefd8191aa1ff3","ma-c-7f1ab7ba65e4b83f7cb3","ma-c-864ac58b3836bb03fb0f","ma-c-8d6fff26008fc8dacac3","ma-c-8f5de9dad5237a0457fe","ma-c-8fd622fcbd3d7dacebf8","ma-c-9b1ce9e20c9744a316da","ma-c-a17f828085d956f5ddcd","ma-c-aa0dad6e82c84b0aeff8","ma-c-c4bfe9579650b815ce8c","ma-c-cd39e53bd9f25e2357eb","ma-c-d9f501651c53edce46fb","ma-c-da7c98c65456ac841089","ma-c-e4a4507d161844c14eca","ma-c-f7b8e207455b3dbfae45","ma-c-fb64a661e711ab32338c"],"papers":{"arXiv:math/0212272":{"abstract":"We study Harish-Chandra representations of Yangian for gl(2). We prove an analogue of Kostant theorem showing that resterited Yangians for gl(2) are free modules over certain maximal commutative subalgebras. We also study the categories of generic Harish-Chandra modules, describe their simple modules and indecomposable modules in tame blocks.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Alexander Molev","Serge Ovsienko"],"year":"2002"},"arXiv:math/0010322":{"abstract":"Let g be an untwisted affine Kac-Moody algebra and M_J(lambda) a Verma-type module for g with J-highest integral weight lambda. We construct quantum Verma-type modules M_J^q(lambda) over the quantum group U_q(g), investigate their properties and show that M_J^q(lambda) is a true quantum deformation of M_J(ł) in the sense that the weight structure is preserved under the deformation. We also analyze","authors":["Vyacheslav M. Futorny","Duncan J. Melville","Alexander N. Grishkov"],"year":"2000"},"arXiv:1906.00385":{"abstract":"For the algebra $I_n$ of polynomial integro-differential operators over a field $K$ of characteristic zero, a classification of simple weight and generalized weight (left and right) $I_n$-modules is given. It is proven that the category of weight $I_n$-modules is semisimple. An explicit description of generalized weight $I_n$-modules is given and using it a criterion is obtained for the problem of","authors":["V. V. Bavula","V. Bekkert","V. Futorny"],"year":"2019"},"arXiv:math/0610071":{"abstract":"We solve the problem of extension of characters of commutative subalgebras in associative (noncommutative) algebras for a class of subrings (Galois orders) in skew group rings. These results can be viewed as a noncommutative analogue of liftings of prime ideals in the case of integral extensions of commutative rings. The proposed approach can be applied to the representation theory of many infinit","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Serge Ovsienko"],"year":"2006"},"arXiv:2112.10911":{"abstract":"This is a survey of some recent progress on quantum symmetric pairs and applications. The topics include quasi K-matrices, $\\imath$Schur duality, canonical bases, super Kazhdan-Lusztig theory, $\\imath$Hall algebras, current presentations for affine $\\imath$quantum groups, and braid group actions.","authors":["Weiqiang Wang"],"year":"2021"},"arXiv:1802.02863":{"abstract":"We construct realizations of quantum generalized Verma modules for U_q(sl_n(C)) by quan- tum differential operators. Taking the classical limit q ! 1 provides a realization of classical generalized Verma modules for sl_n(C) by differential operators.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Libor Krizka","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2018"},"arXiv:0801.0903":{"abstract":"We address two problems regarding the structure and representation theory of finite W-algebras associated with the general linear Lie algebras. Finite W-algebras can be defined either via the Whittaker model of Kostant or, equivalently, by the quantum Hamiltonian reduction. Our first main result is a proof of the Gelfand-Kirillov conjecture for the skew fields of fractions of the finite W-algebras","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Alexander Molev","Serge Ovsienko"],"year":"2008"},"arXiv:0711.0793":{"abstract":"We show that if A is an abelian category satisfying certain mild conditions, then one can introduce the concept of a moduli space of (semi)stable objects which has the structure of a projective algebraic variety. This idea is applied to several important abelian categories in representation theory, like highest weight categories.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Marcos Jardim","Adriano Moura"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:1806.07519":{"abstract":"Truncated shifted Yangians are a family of algebras which naturally quantize slices in the affine Grassmannian. These algebras depend on a choice of two weights $λ$ and $μ$ for a Lie algebra $\\mathfrak{g}$, which we will assume is simply-laced. In this paper, we relate the category $\\mathcal{O}$ over truncated shifted Yangians to categorified tensor products: for a generic integral choice of param","authors":["Joel Kamnitzer","Peter Tingley","Ben Webster"],"year":"2018"},"arXiv:math/0610069":{"abstract":"We introduce and develop a structure theory of a new class of noncommutative rings - Galois orders, that generalize classical orders in noncommutative rings. Galois orders realized as certain subrings of invariants in skew semigroup rings. This class of rings contains many classical objects, in particular the Generalized Weyl algebras, the universal enveloping algebra of the general linear Lie alg","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Serge Ovsienko"],"year":"2006"},"arXiv:2507.10782":{"abstract":"Galois rings and Galois orders, introduced by Futorny and Ovsienko, are realized as subrings of fixed subrings of skew group (or monoid) rings and have numerous applications in the structure and representation theory of associative algebras. This paper consists of two parts. The first parte investigates ring-theoretic properties that follow from the Galois ring structure alone. In particular, we e","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Jonas T. Hartwig","Erich C. Jauch"],"year":"2025"},"arXiv:2006.05618":{"abstract":"We classify all simple strong Harish-Chandra modules for the Lie superalgebra $W(m,n)$. We show that every such module is either strongly cuspidal or a module of the highest weight type. We construct tensor modules for $W(m,n)$, which are parametrized by simple finite-dimensional $gl(m,n)$-modules and show that every simple strongly cuspidal $W(m,n)$-module is a quotient of a tensor module. Finall","authors":["Yuly Billig","Vyacheslav Futorny","Kenji Iohara"],"year":"2020"}}}